# What must not enter the production build context.
#
# There was no .dockerignore until 11.3, and `COPY . .` in Dockerfile.prod therefore
# copied the whole working tree. Inspecting the built image found two things in it that
# the Dockerfile's own comments promised were not:
#
#   1. **`.env`** — the developer's local secrets, baked into an artefact that goes to a
#      registry. The image header says "no secrets of any kind"; it was wrong, and
#      nothing would have said so.
#   2. **`vendor/pestphp`** — the local vendor tree, complete with dev dependencies.
#      `COPY --from=vendor /build/vendor ./vendor` *merges* into an existing directory
#      rather than replacing it, so `--no-dev` bought nothing: Pest, Larastan, Mockery
#      and Faker all shipped, and the production autoloader could reach them.
#
# It is also most of the image size: node_modules and .git are pure context.

# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example

# --- built or installed inside the image, in their own stages ----------------
vendor/
node_modules/
public/build/
public/hot

# --- history and tooling -----------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.githooks/
.github/
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- not shipped -------------------------------------------------------------
docs/
tests/
release/
certbot/
compose.yaml
compose.prod.yaml
Makefile
phpunit.xml
phpstan.neon.dist
pint.json
*.md

# --- runtime state, recreated by the app -------------------------------------
storage/logs/*
storage/framework/cache/data/*
storage/framework/sessions/*
storage/framework/views/*
storage/app/public/*
bootstrap/cache/*

# --- local noise -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.phpunit.result.cache
